# libusb

ArchiveTune's retained Android sources are normalized to stable libusb 1.0.30,
tag `v1.0.30`, commit `87a55632db62c9bdc58cd31d3ccfa673f1bb017f`
(https://github.com/libusb/libusb/tree/v1.0.30), verified on 2026-10-14.
The previous vendor tree was an untagged pre-final snapshot, not a clean rc1.
`libusb/descriptor.c`, `io.c`, `libusbi.h`, `version.h` and `version_nano.h`
were refreshed together with the upstream ChangeLog; the other selected
Linux/POSIX sources and public header already matched stable. ArchiveTune's
Android configuration and explicit application CMake source selection are retained.
This is retained-source provenance, not a claim that every upstream platform or
build file was replaced.

libusb is a library for USB device access from Linux, macOS,
Windows, OpenBSD/NetBSD, Haiku, Solaris userspace, and WebAssembly
via WebUSB.
It is written in C (Haiku backend in C++) and licensed under the GNU
Lesser General Public License version 2.1 or, at your option, any later
version (see [COPYING](COPYING)).

libusb is abstracted internally in such a way that it can hopefully
be ported to other operating systems. Please see the [PORTING](PORTING)
file for more information.

libusb homepage:
https://libusb.info/

Developers will wish to consult the API documentation:
http://api.libusb.info

Use the mailing list for questions, comments, etc:
http://mailing-list.libusb.info

